        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "3. Old before new. Begin sentences with familiar information; end them with information readers cannot predict.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                117,
                771,
                166
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1,
            "group_id": 2,
            "global_block_id": 2,
            "global_group_id": 2,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    117.0
                ],
                [
                    771.0,
                    166.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    166.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "4. Simple before complex. Open with simple concepts or grammatical units; put more complex concepts or grammatical units later in the sentence, where readers can handle them better.",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
                175,
                772,
                250
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 3,
            "global_block_id": 3,
            "global_group_id": 3,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    79.0,
                    175.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    175.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    250.0
                ],
                [
                    79.0,
                    250.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "5. Short before long. Begin with a short, easily grasped segment of information that frames the longer, more complex segments that follow. This principle applies not only to sentences but also to paragraphs, sections, and whole documents.",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                259,
                772,
                359
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 4,
            "global_block_id": 4,
            "global_group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    259.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    259.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    359.0
                ],
                [
                    80.0,
                    359.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "6. Begin with the topic. Begin your sentences by announcing their topics, what they are \"about\" or \"comment on.\"",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                369,
                772,
                419
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 5,
            "global_block_id": 5,
            "global_group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    80.0,
                    369.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    369.0
                ],
                [
                    772.0,
                    419.0
                ],
                [
                    80.0,
                    419.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "7. End on stress. End your sentences with words that should receive special emphasis.",
            "block_bbox": [
                80,
                427,
                772,
                477
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 6,
            "global_block_id": 6,
            "global_group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
